ADJUDICATION (same session): the model is residual-adequate on all six
runs but its parameters are DEGENERATE -- s1 ~ +1.2e4 with w ~ 0.2 and
center below the data window means the optimizer repurposed the tanh into
"deep slope + exponentially decaying transient": slope(x) ~ s2 +
s1 exp(-2(x-x0)/w). s1, x0, w are NOT individually physical; do not quote
them as observables. Robust extracts, consistent across all six runs
after A0 rescaling:
  (1) deep asymptote s2 = -1.07 +- 0.03 (slightly shallower than the
      top-half chord values -1.12..-1.29 -- the chords likely average
      residual transient; both quoted, neither replaces the other);
  (2) fit-implied slope zero crossing 48.8-50.5 x A0, systematically ~8%
      below the direct estimator's 54 x A0 -- two estimators, one
      invariant, small methodical offset, both A0-linear;
  (3) SWITCH SHARPNESS: the transient decays with e-folding scale w/2 ~
      0.1 in ln A -- the slope goes from 0 to ~-1 within ~0.2-0.3 e-folds
      of amplitude. The viscous inversion is close to a STEP at the fixed
      growth factor. [The "dynamical age trigger" gloss written here was
subsequently RETRACTED; see B_BAND.out SELF-AUDIT CORRECTION: the trigger
is 1.43x above the IC corner-gradient value.]
The universal object is the whole rescaled curve sigma(A/A0), not any
single fitted parameter.
